      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiC-ZrB2 composite will achieve improved densification relative to single-phase ZrB2.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiC-ZrB2 composite will have reduced porosity relative to single-phase ZrB2.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC acts as a sintering aid in ZrB2.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC promotes lower-temperature densification by enhancing mass transport.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiC promotes lower-temperature densification by reducing grain-boundary energy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiC phase fills voids in the ZrB2 matrix.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiC phase inhibits the formation of interconnected porosity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced interconnected porosity increases resistance to penetration by the liquid plating bath.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced liquid penetration limits mechanical degradation during service.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A 5-10 wt% SiC addition will reduce the required ZrB2 preparation temperature by 100-200 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiC-ZrB2 composite will retain better structural integrity during prolonged plating-bath exposure than conventionally prepared single-phase ZrB2.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed preparation window is 2000-2300 °C for ZrB2 containing 5-10 wt% SiC.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism is applicable only when the liquid plating bath does not chemically degrade SiC.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Samples with and without SiC should be prepared below 2300 °C and compared using relative density, porosity, flexural strength, crack density, weight loss, and mechanical-property retention after bath exposure.",
